protocol "PBM — Anxiety (Wang 2023, high-irradiance)" {
    id: "30000051-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
    description: "820nm PBM to the left DLPFC for generalized anxiety, as Wang 2023 ran it (double-blind sham-controlled RCT, n=36, 33 analysed): a continuous-wave laser at 310 mW/cm², a 1 cm spot at F5, four 4-minute exposures a day 5 minutes apart, on 14 consecutive days. HAMA fell more than sham (p=0.021) and stayed lower at 8 weeks; HAMA response 11/16 active vs 2/17 sham. Grade B. One session here is one day of that course; the 14-day schedule is the user's to keep, since the language has no course field. REFUSED ON THIS HARDWARE TODAY: the validator still caps duty at 25% (OI-HEXTILE-31) and U4 cannot yet conduct CW (OI-HEXTILE-30). It is not reshaped to fit. 310 mW/cm² CW is inside the time-averaged ceiling at 820nm (≈348, CLAUDE.md §3)."
    author: "NeurOne"
    version: "2.1"
    readonly: true
    tags: ["pbm", "clinical", "anxiety", "dlpfc", "cw", "wang2023"]
    conditions: ["Generalized Anxiety Disorder"]
    references: [["Wang H, Song P et al. 2023, Brain Res Bull 200:110682, doi:10.1016/j.brainresbull.2023.110682 — double-blind sham-controlled RCT, n=36 (16 active and 17 sham completed); 820nm diverging continuous laser, 310 mW/cm², 1 cm diameter spot at F5 (left DLPFC); 4 × 4 min daily at 5-min intervals, 16 min/day, 14 consecutive days; HAMA reduced vs sham (p=0.021), sustained to the 8-week follow-up. THIS protocol's source (§2.2 of the paper).", "docs/pbm_neuro_protocols.md#5-anxiety--gad--grade-b"], ["PBM protocol database §5 — Anxiety / GAD (Grade B)", "docs/pbm_neuro_protocols.md#5-anxiety--gad--grade-b"]]
    duration: 31m

    # Everything below is from §2.2 of the paper (read 2026-09-29), except
    # where marked.
    #
    # Timing: four 4-min exposures with 5 min between them. The last off-period
    # falls after the session ends, so the session is 4 × 4 + 3 × 5 = 31 min.
    #
    # Dose at the scalp: 310 mW/cm² × 240 s = 74.4 J/cm² per exposure,
    # 297.6 J/cm² per day. (The paper's 10.4 J is its own estimate of energy at
    # the cortex: 4.5 % transmission over the 0.785 cm² spot.)
    #
    # Why this is refused, and why it is left refused. CLAUDE.md §3: a PBM
    # ceiling refuses a protocol and never reshapes one. v1.0 and v2.0 of this
    # file ran 10 Hz at 25 % duty for 7 min, which is not what Wang tested.
    # The average term allows 310 at 820nm (200 × C_A ≈ 348; NP-HW-HEXTILE-001
    # D-10); the 400 peak is not reached. What refuses it is the
    # validator's 25 % duty cap (OI-HEXTILE-31) and U4 (OI-HEXTILE-30).

    pbm_transcranial {
        wavelength: "820nm"
        # The default wavelength rules deliver 820nm on the 808nm channel alone
        # (NP-NPPS-REF-001 §4.1a).
        frequency: 0Hz
        duty_cycle: 100%
        intensity: 77%
        # PROVISIONAL, NOT THE AUTHORED VALUE: 310 ÷ 403 against the only
        # stated anchor (NP-HW-HEXTILE-001 §4.3.1), which NP-SES-PWR-001 §2.3
        # flags as an "if". Becomes `irradiance_mw_cm2: 310`.
        zones: ["Frontal Left (excl. midline)"]
        # Site fidelity gap. Wang treated F5 — between F3 and F7 — with a
        # 0.785 cm² spot. This zone is 17 modules, so it lights several hundred
        # times the trial's area (OI-SESPWR-01). Whether F5 lies inside this
        # zone or at its temporal edge is not known until the sockets are
        # registered to 10-20 sites (REG-1). The midline sockets are omitted so
        # the left-only target does not spill into the right hemisphere
        # (NP-OPT-PSF-001 §4).
        #
        # Source difference: the trial used a laser; the tile uses LEDs.
        interval_on: 4m
        interval_off: 5m
        repeat: 4
    }
}
